# Old Wix URLs -> current structure. Copied to the publish root by
# scripts/build.mjs and read by Cloudflare's asset server.
#
# CONSTRAINTS OF THIS FILE — it is validated server-side at DEPLOY time, and a
# single bad line fails the whole deploy, not just that rule.
#   - Only 301, 302, 303, 307 and 308 are accepted. 410 is NOT supported.
#   - The source must be a path. Hostname sources are NOT supported, which is
#     why apex -> www lives in worker/index.js instead.
#   - Netlify's `301!` force suffix parses as status 0 here. Do not use it.
# `wrangler deploy --dry-run` does NOT catch violations; the first sign is a
# failed build.
#
# These URLs carry no link equity — every measured backlink points at the root,
# none at any inner page. They are mapped for index-transition hygiene and for
# anyone following an old bookmark, not to recover authority.
#
# Deliberately absent: /items, /event-list, /event-details/*,
# /donation-thank-you-page, /blog and /rental. Those are unused Wix template
# leftovers that never had anything to do with cranes. They 404 today and stay
# that way, with matching Disallow lines in robots.txt. A 410 would be more
# precise but this file cannot express one.

# --- Top-level pages -------------------------------------------------------
